# Repository Structure

## Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture Engineering Repository – Public (AER-PU)

---

## Purpose

The purpose of this document is to define the organizational structure of the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture Engineering Repository – Public (AER-PU). It establishes how approved engineering knowledge is organized, stored, maintained, and navigated throughout the lifecycle of the AVIA project.

---

# Repository Organization Philosophy

The repository shall be organized as an engineering knowledge system rather than a collection of unrelated files.

Every document shall occupy a defined location within the repository hierarchy according to its engineering purpose and relationship to other engineering knowledge.

The repository structure shall promote:

- Clarity
- Traceability
- Scalability
- Maintainability
- Consistency
- Discoverability

---

# Repository Architecture

The repository is organized into two primary layers:

## Layer 1 – Repository Governance

This layer contains documents that govern the operation of the repository itself.

Examples include:

- README.md
- GOVERNANCE.md
- CONTRIBUTING.md
- CHANGELOG.md

---

## Layer 2 – Engineering Knowledge

This layer contains approved engineering knowledge relating to the AVIA project.

Examples include:

- Project Charter
- System Specifications
- Engineering Architectures
- Engineering Principles
- Engineering Laws
- Validation Reports
- Technical Documentation

---

# Top-Level Repository Structure

The repository shall follow the following high-level organization:

```text
AER-PU/

README.md
GOVERNANCE.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CHANGELOG.md

docs/

archive/

resources/
```

---

# Engineering Knowledge Structure

The `docs/` directory shall contain organized engineering knowledge.

A typical structure shall include:

```text
docs/

Project_Charter/

System_Objective_Specification/

System_Requirements_Specification/

Functional_Architecture/

Physics_Architecture/

Mathematical_Architecture/

Decision_Architecture/

Control_Architecture/

Mechanical_Architecture/

Electrical_Architecture/

Simulation/

Testing/

Validation/

Engineering_Principles/

Engineering_Laws/

Glossary/
```

The structure may expand as the AVIA project evolves while preserving consistency and traceability.

---

# Archive Structure

The `archive/` directory shall preserve superseded engineering knowledge.

Archived documents shall remain available for historical reference and engineering traceability.

Documents shall not be permanently removed when replaced by newer approved versions unless required by repository governance.

---

# Resources Structure

The `resources/` directory shall contain supporting materials that assist in understanding the repository.

Examples include:

- Repository images
- Diagrams
- Figures
- Templates
- Reference material

Resources shall support engineering documentation but shall not replace official engineering documents.

---

# Repository Navigation Principles

The repository shall be organized so that:

- Similar engineering knowledge is grouped together.
- Repository navigation remains intuitive.
- Engineering documents remain easy to locate.
- Repository growth does not require major structural redesign.

---

# Repository Growth Policy

The repository structure is intended to support long-term expansion.

New engineering domains may be added when justified by the evolution of the AVIA project.

Expansion shall preserve the existing organizational philosophy and maintain repository consistency.

---

# Repository Maintenance

The repository structure shall be periodically reviewed to ensure it continues to support the engineering needs of the AVIA project.

Structural improvements shall be introduced through controlled governance and documented within the repository changelog.

---

# Repository Philosophy

A repository is not simply a storage location.

It is the architectural framework through which engineering knowledge is organized, preserved, and communicated.

The structure of the repository should reflect the structure of the engineering system it documents.

